  "question": {
    "text": "A disc of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is attached to a rectangular plate of the same mass, breadth <math><mi>R</mi></math> and length <math><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></math> as shown in figure. The moment of inertia of the system about the axis <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> passing through the centre of the disc and along the plane is <math><mi>Ι</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>31</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>, where value of <math><mi>α</mi></math>&nbsp;is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0076_da2f632a7274.png\" style=\"width: 130px; height: 141px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
